Title:
COMouflage: Stealthy DLL Surrogate Injection for Process Tree Evasion

Type:
Blog Post

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- This post describes “COMouflage,” a Windows code-execution/injection technique that abuses COM DLL Surrogates to load an attacker-controlled DLL inside `dllhost.exe`.  
- It solves the problem of noisy classic injection (e.g., `CreateRemoteThread`, `WriteProcessMemory`) and suspicious parent/child lineage by making `svchost.exe` appear as the parent of the surrogate-hosted `dllhost.exe`.  
- The technique registers a fake COM object under `HKCU\Software\Classes\{AppID,CLSID}` (no admin required), sets `AppID\DllSurrogate` to an empty string (default surrogate), and points `CLSID\InprocServer32` to the payload DLL.  
- Execution is triggered via `CoCreateInstance` with `CLSCTX_LOCAL_SERVER`, causing COM SCM to spawn `dllhost.exe` and load the DLL “legitimately.”  
- The article includes a C++ PoC, notes low AV/EDR detection in the author’s testing, and provides a YARA rule focused on registry/API indicators.  
- Useful primarily for red teams and malware developers; also relevant to blue teams for hunting COM surrogate abuse and anomalous `dllhost.exe` instantiation patterns.

Technical Focus:
- COM DLL Surrogate mechanism (`DllSurrogate`) abuse
- HKCU COM registration hijacking (`Software\Classes\AppID` / `Software\Classes\CLSID`)
- Process tree / parent process masquerading (`svchost.exe` → `dllhost.exe`)
- COM activation via `CoCreateInstance` + `CLSCTX_LOCAL_SERVER`
- Windows Registry manipulation APIs (`RegCreateKeyExW`, `RegSetValueExW`)
- Detection ideas (YARA, behavioral lineage anomalies)

Use Cases:
- Stealthy user-level code execution inside `dllhost.exe` without direct remote-thread injection
- Process lineage evasion against detections relying on parent/child relationships
- Tradecraft for living-off-the-land style execution using COM infrastructure
- Defensive hunting for suspicious per-user COM registrations and surrogate activations

Keywords:
COM, DLL Surrogate, DllSurrogate, dllhost.exe, svchost.exe, COM SCM, CoCreateInstance, CLSCTX_LOCAL_SERVER, CLSID, AppID, InprocServer32, HKCU, Software\Classes, COM hijacking, process tree evasion, parent PID spoofing, Windows Registry, RegCreateKeyExW, RegSetValueExW, ThreadingModel Apartment, YARA, T1546.015